# Render Static Site routing (Netlify-style _redirects).
#
# IMPORTANT: Render's static site _redirects parser ONLY supports SPA
# fallback (200-status rewrites) when the destination is /index.html.
# Rewriting to /app.html (or any other path) is silently ignored —
# which is why deep links like /supplierManagement or /loginUni
# previously 404'd on reload.
#
# This file is structured around that constraint:
#
#   - /                → /landing.html    200   (marketing page)
#   - /app.html        → real file (SPA shell, kept for backwards-compat
#                       with /app.html?route=... deep links)
#   - /index.html      → real file (the SPA shell — Render's SPA
#                       fallback destination)
#   - /landing.html    → real file (marketing page)
#   - everything else   → /index.html    200   (SPA fallback so the
#                       Flutter router handles client-side routes
#                       like /supplierManagement, /loginUni,
#                       /registerUni, /resetPasswordUni, etc.)
#
# This file MUST live in the published directory (build/web/_redirects).
# build.sh copies it in after `flutter build web`.

# Root URL serves the marketing landing page (rewrite, not redirect —
# the browser URL stays at /, so the user sees a clean URL).
/                /landing.html   200

# Any other non-file path falls through to the SPA shell, which
# Flutter's router then handles client-side. This is Render's
# documented SPA fallback pattern.
/*               /index.html     200
